;: 1,\n        \&quot;erasableAt\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;erasableBy\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;createdAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T06:59:25.755Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;createdBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T09:10:52.016Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;\n      },\n      {\n        \&quot;id\&quot;: \&quot;ad_ae39d85b-d291-4a20-93df-8df8a39e80eb\&quot;,\n        \&quot;projectId\&quot;: \&quot;cmqeu7cr1000batte885ajo20\&quot;,\n        \&quot;label\&quot;: \&quot;Rosette punch-mark decoration\&quot;,\n        \&quot;description\&quot;: \&quot;Rosette-shaped punch-mark decoration executed from the recto of the sheet. Due to the extremely thin silver foil, the operation was likely performed with the metal embedded in a pitch support (chasing pitch), which allowed the punch to impress the motif without folding or tearing the sheet. The regular morphology of the rosette suggests the use of a purpose-made punch.\&quot;,\n        \&quot;class\&quot;: \&quot;ocra-voc:rosette\&quot;,\n        \&quot;content\&quot;: {},\n        \&quot;visibilityType\&quot;: \&quot;scene\&quot;,\n        \&quot;visibilityId\&quot;: \&quot;scene_1781505241833\&quot;,\n        \&quot;version\&quot;: 2,\n        \&quot;erasableAt\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;erasableBy\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;createdAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T07:07:29.672Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;createdBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T09:43:42.705Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;\n      },\n      {\n        \&quot;id\&quot;: \&quot;ad_ae9c9514-538d-4155-9c16-67be4998bccb\&quot;,\n        \&quot;projectId\&quot;: \&quot;cmqeu7cr1000batte885ajo20\&quot;,\n        \&quot;label\&quot;: \&quot;Lacuna\&quot;,\n        \&quot;description\&quot;: \&quot;\&quot;,\n        \&quot;class\&quot;: \&quot;ocra-voc:lacuna\&quot;,\n        \&quot;content\&quot;: {},\n        \&quot;visibilityType\&quot;: \&quot;scene\&quot;,\n        \&quot;visibilityId\&quot;: \&quot;scene_1781505241833\&quot;,\n        \&quot;version\&quot;: 1,\n        \&quot;erasableAt\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;erasableBy\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;createdAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T07:01:04.531Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;createdBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T09:13:28.611Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;\n      },\n      {\n        \&quot;id\&quot;: \&quot;ad_b24dc6c0-ec8e-46bf-85a6-9192b1c423e3\&quot;,\n        \&quot;projectId\&quot;: \&quot;cmqeu7cr1000batte885ajo20\&quot;,\n        \&quot;label\&quot;: \&quot;Lacuna\&quot;,\n        \&quot;description\&quot;: \&quot;\&quot;,\n        \&quot;class\&quot;: \&quot;ocra-voc:lacuna\&quot;,\n        \&quot;content\&quot;: {},\n        \&quot;visibilityType\&quot;: \&quot;scene\&quot;,\n        \&quot;visibilityId\&quot;: \&quot;scene_1781505241833\&quot;,\n        \&quot;version\&quot;: 1,\n        \&quot;erasableAt\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;erasableBy\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;createdAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T07:02:04.788Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;createdBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T09:14:07.922Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;\n      },\n      {\n        \&quot;id\&quot;: \&quot;ad_b5df7e98-78f7-4244-a3f4-3f744219c884\&quot;,\n        \&quot;projectId\&quot;: \&quot;cmqeu7cr1000batte885ajo20\&quot;,\n        \&quot;label\&quot;: \&quot;Fracture\&quot;,\n        \&quot;description\&quot;: \&quot;\&quot;,\n        \&quot;class\&quot;: \&quot;ocra-voc:fracture\&quot;,\n        \&quot;content\&quot;: {},\n        \&quot;visibilityType\&quot;: \&quot;scene\&quot;,\n        \&quot;visibilityId\&quot;: \&quot;scene_1781505241833\&quot;,\n        \&quot;version\&quot;: 1,\n        \&quot;erasableAt\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;erasableBy\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;createdAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T07:02:37.702Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;createdBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T09:14:32.040Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;\n      },\n      {\n        \&quot;id\&quot;: \&quot;ad_d24b60b4-0593-4c3c-a604-ff0f8573da35\&quot;,\n        \&quot;projectId\&quot;: \&quot;cmqeu7cr1000batte885ajo20\&quot;,\n        \&quot;label\&quot;: \&quot;Egyptianizing Uraei\&quot;,\n        \&quot;description\&quot;: \&quot;Pair of uraei flanking the solar disk. The snakes are represented in the characteristic Egyptian manner as rearing cobras with expanded hoods, symmetrically arranged on either side of the disk. This iconographic scheme is strongly Egyptianizing and recalls royal and divine symbols widely used in ancient Egyptian art, where the uraeus represented protection, sovereignty, and divine authority. The association of the solar disk with paired uraei is a well-established motif in Egyptian religious iconography and reflects the close cultural interactions between the Punic and Egyptian worlds.\&quot;,\n        \&quot;class\&quot;: \&quot;ocra-voc:uraeus\&quot;,\n        \&quot;content\&quot;: {},\n        \&quot;visibilityType\&quot;: \&quot;scene\&quot;,\n        \&quot;visibilityId\&quot;: \&quot;scene_1781505241833\&quot;,\n        \&quot;version\&quot;: 1,\n        \&quot;erasableAt\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;erasableBy\&quot;: null,\n        \&quot;createdAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T07:07:38.605Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;createdBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedAt\&quot;: \&quot;2026-06-15T09:40:03.755Z\&quot;,\n        \&quot;updatedBy\&quot;: \&quot;cmpdyui3t0000lxshmqc2zlp2\&qu