      },
      {
        &quot;id&quot;: &quot;ad_ae39d85b-d291-4a20-93df-8df8a39e80eb&quot;,
        &quot;projectId&quot;: &quot;cmqeu7cr1000batte885ajo20&quot;,
        &quot;label&quot;: &quot;Rosette punch-mark decoration&quot;,
        &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Rosette-shaped punch-mark decoration executed from the recto of the sheet. Due to the extremely thin silver foil, the operation was likely performed with the metal embedded in a pitch support (chasing pitch), which allowed the punch to impress the motif without folding or tearing the sheet. The regular morphology of the rosette suggests the use of a purpose-made punch.&quot;,
        &quot;class&quot;: &quot;ocra-voc:rosette&quot;,
        &quot;content&quot;: {},
        &quot;visibilityType&quot;: &quot;scene&quot;,
